## EcosystemApp interface

```typescript
interface EcosystemApp {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  tagline: string;
  description: string;
  role: "control-tower" | "product" | "infrastructure" | "integration";
  status: "active" | "development" | "planned";
  repo: string;           // GitHub URL
  stack: string[];
  agents: string[];       // linked agent names
  healthPath?: string;    // e.g. "/api/health"
  defaultUrl?: string;
  envKey?: string;        // VITE_*_URL for client
  color: string;
  icon: string;
}
```

## API

- `GET /api/ecosystem` — all apps with live health status
- `GET /api/ecosystem/apps` — list without health ping
- `GET /api/ecosystem/:id` — single app detail + health

## Ecosystem page

`/ecosystem` — grid of product cards with health dots, repo links, agent badges.
Pings each app's `healthPath` on defaultUrl.

## Cross-app env vars

Products can be linked via Vite env:
- `VITE_NIRVAPROCURE_URL`
- `VITE_NIRVASELL_URL`
- etc. (see ecosystem.ts envKey per app)

## Integration pattern

1. Register app in `shared/ecosystem.ts`
2. Add health ping in `server/ecosystem/index.ts`
3. Display on Ecosystem page
4. Route agent tasks to external app APIs via plugins or workflows

